{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For the wheat and the spelt were late.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): because they were late (אפילות) and had not yet grown, therefore they were not struck." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> כי אפילות הנה — wonders upon wonders were wrought in them. And the explanation of this is that they were not spared from the plague because they were late-growing (אפילות), for given the severity of the plague of hail and the force of its cold it would have been fitting that the roots of the grain should die beneath the ground, or given the strength of the kindled fire that they should be burned; but it was by way of miracle, and wonders were performed in them — and this is the sense of כי אפילות הנה: read it as כי פלאות הנה — 'for wonders are these.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:17.284446683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}